{"name":"Mineral Spring","hex":"#edf2ec","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mineral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any naturally occurring solid material that has a (more or less) definite chemical composition and characteristic physical properties; especially, an inorganic and crystalline one.","Any inorganic material (as distinguished from animal or vegetable)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["of, related to, or containing minerals"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mineral"},{"term":"spring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move or burst forth.","To appear."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of springing: a leap, a jump.","The season of the year in temperate regions in which temperatures and daylight hours rise, and plants spring from the ground and into bloom and dormant animals spring to life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mineral spring","blocks":[{"text":"Mineral springs are naturally occurring springs that produce hard water, water that contains dissolved minerals. Salts, sulfur compounds, and gases are among the substances that can be dissolved in the spring water during its passage underground. In this they are unlike sweet springs, which produce soft water with no noticeable dissolved gasses. The dissolved minerals may alter the water's taste. Mineral water obtained from mineral springs, and the precipitated salts such as Epsom salt have long been important commercial products."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Wenceslas_Hollar_-_The_mineral_spring_%28State_4%29.jpg/330px-Wenceslas_Hollar_-_The_mineral_spring_%28State_4%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mineral_spring","wikidata":"Q1365924"},{"title":"Mineral Spring, Missouri","blocks":[{"text":"Mineral Spring is an unincorporated community in Barry County, in the U.S. state of Missouri."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mineral_Spring%2C_Missouri","wikidata":"Q27983875"},{"title":"Mineral","blocks":[{"text":"In geology and mineralogy, a mineral or mineral species is, broadly speaking, a solid substance with a fairly well-defined chemical composition and a specific crystal structure that occurs naturally in pure form."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/S%C3%A9randite%2C_natrolite%2C_analcime%2C_aegirine_300-4-2112.JPG/330px-S%C3%A9randite%2C_natrolite%2C_analcime%2C_aegirine_300-4-2112.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mineral","wikidata":"Q7946"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Hot_springs_at_Manikaran%2CHimachal_Pradesh.jpg/500px-Hot_springs_at_Manikaran%2CHimachal_Pradesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Hot_springs_at_Manikaran%2CHimachal_Pradesh.jpg/1280px-Hot_springs_at_Manikaran%2CHimachal_Pradesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Hot_springs_at_Manikaran%2CHimachal_Pradesh.jpg/500px-Hot_springs_at_Manikaran%2CHimachal_Pradesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tourists and pilgrims having a bath in a hot spring in Gurudwara Complex, Manikaran in Himachal Pradesh state of India, c. May 2009.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHot_springs_at_Manikaran%2CHimachal_Pradesh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Breznik-iron-water-spring.jpg/500px-Breznik-iron-water-spring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Breznik-iron-water-spring.jpg/1280px-Breznik-iron-water-sp